public with sharing class HouseholdService {

    public static Id createHousehold(List<Contact> members) {
        if (members == null || members.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException('members must not be null or empty');
        }

        // Resolve the Household Account record type without hard-coding the Id
        Id hhRecordTypeId = Schema.SObjectType.Account
            .getRecordTypeInfosByDeveloperName()
            .get('HH_Account')
            .getRecordTypeId();

        // Provide a placeholder Name to satisfy the required-field check at DML time.
        // NPSP's after-insert trigger on Contact will overwrite it with the real
        // household name (and greetings) once the members are linked.
        Account household = new Account(
            RecordTypeId = hhRecordTypeId,
            Name         = 'Household'
        );
        insert household;

        // Assign every member to the single household and bulk-insert in one DML.
        // This fires NPSP's household-naming trigger, which replaces the placeholder
        // Name with a properly formatted household name.
        for (Contact c : members) {
            c.AccountId = household.Id;
        }
        insert members;

        // Set the first contact as the household's 1-to-1 primary contact.
        // Use a targeted update (only Id + the field we care about) so we do not
        // clobber the Name that NPSP just generated.  NPSP re-runs household naming
        // on this update because npe01__One2OneContact__c changed.
        Account primaryUpdate = new Account(
            Id                          = household.Id,
            npe01__One2OneContact__c    = members[0].Id
        );
        update primaryUpdate;

        return household.Id;
    }
}
```

**What changed and why:**

| Issue | Fix |
|---|---|
| `Account.Name` is a **required** field; inserting without it throws `REQUIRED_FIELD_MISSING` before any trigger can run. | Insert the Account with a short placeholder `Name = 'Household'`. NPSP's after-insert trigger on Contact fires when the members are linked and overwrites the placeholder with the real household name. |
| A full `update household` would send the stale in-memory `Name` back and clobber the NPSP-generated name. | Perform a **targeted update** (`new Account(Id = …, npe01__One2OneContact__c = …)`) so only the primary-contact field is written. NPSP's naming trigger re-fires on this update and regenerates the name/greetings correctly. |
| No empty or extra accounts left behind | Still exactly one Account DML insert; any failure rolls back the whole synchronous transaction. |
| No hard-coded record-type Ids | Resolved at runtime via `getRecordTypeInfosByDeveloperName()`. |

