### Why this satisfies every requirement

| Requirement | How it is met |
|---|---|
| **`with sharing`** | Declared on the class, so OWD = Private and sharing rules are enforced at the record level. No `without sharing` override. |
| **No sharing bypass** | No `@AuraEnabled(cacheable=true)`, no `Security.stripInaccessible` to hide the fact, no `without sharing` sub-method. The SOQL runs in the running user's sharing context. |
| **Field-level security** | Each of the three custom fields is tested with `DescribeFieldResult.isAccessible()` **before** being added to the query string. Fields the user cannot read are simply **never queried**, so they are **absent** from the returned SObject records (not set, not null). |
| **Must not throw on missing FLS** | Because inaccessible fields are excluded from the SELECT list, the SOQL engine never encounters a field the user can't read, so no `QueryException` is raised. |
| **Object-level read check** | `SObjectType.isAccessible()` returns `false` when the user lacks the object's "Read" permission, and we return an empty list immediately. |
| **Ordering** | `ORDER BY Name ASC` in every variant of the dynamic query. |
| **Bulk-safe** | Single query, no per-record DML, no per-record describe calls inside a loop (all describes are done once before the query). |

